    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's just a way to comfort ourselves, isn't it? pretending there's meaning just because we're here right now. if we look at it purely through the lens of entropy, everything we build, every effort we make to \"find purpose,\" is just fighting a losing battle against the inevitable. \n\nit feels like we're just forcing ourselves to stay in a state of high tension and effort when the most natural state for anything is to just... stop. to reach equilibrium. why is it considered \"good\" to resist that? it feels like staying alive is just an unnecessary expenditure of energy against the natural order of things.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
